WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.702
[music playing]

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.770
[ding]

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.646
INTERVIEWER: (VOICEOVER) One of
the big players in that world,

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.782
someone I'm told moves
more than a million

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:22.088
worth of product daily,
has agreed to meet me--

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:25.058
well, kind of.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.226
INTERVIEWER: OK, we ready?

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.794
GEORGE: Yep.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:32.632
So I'm currently in an empty
room and in front of a table

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:36.236
with nine pounds of all sorts
of different kinds of weed.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.771
George, I'm just
explaining what's

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.305
happening to the cameras.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.273
Because it feels really weird
that it's just me here so

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.074
I'm just explaining.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.275
GEORGE: Yep.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.376
INTERVIEWER: (VOICEOVER)
George didn't

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.878
want his actual voice recorded.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:48.381
George is actually
out of view.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:51.151
He didn't feel comfortable
being on camera,

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.685
but he can hear me
because of my mic.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.988
INTERVIEWER: (VOICEOVER) So
we're using a voice changer

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.689
that alters it while he speaks.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.992
If I were a buyer,
I would come in here.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.760
You'd have all
these bags out here

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.195
with the different samples.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:06.266
They'd look at it, smell it,
possibly try it, smoke it.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.301
GEORGE: Some will smoke
it, but it's really just,

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.003
you know, based off
the smell, mainly

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.906
the smell, then the look.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.040
And then they place orders.

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:14.974
Is that it?

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.142
GEORGE: Yep.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.610
INTERVIEWER:
(VOICEOVER) On the table

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:21.681
is a variety of high end
exotic indoor and outdoor weed.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:26.352
Each pound bag costs
between $2,000 and $4,000.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:29.789
What's the largest order
you've ever received?

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.559
GEORGE: I mean, they'll go
up to hundreds of pounds.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.894
INTERVIEWER: (VOICEOVER)
Just one order that size is

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.497
worth around a million dollars.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.098
INTERVIEWER: How
much money is there

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.167
to be made in illegal weed?

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.870
GEORGE: Oh, endless,
endless amounts.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:47.540
I shouldn't really be
talking about this to someone

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.209
for camera.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.578
INTERVIEWER: (VOICEOVER)
I decide not to push it.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:55.215
So George, you operate
just a black market business?

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.484
Or do you operate
also a legal business?

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.185
GEORGE: Licensed as well.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.753
Licensed as well.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:04.858
If you were to give me a general
sense of how much money you

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:07.627
make with your legal versus
your illegal business,

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.762
what would you say?

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.965
GEORGE: Well, technically,
I haven't made profit

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.601
off my legal business yet.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:15.602
Wow.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.639
GEORGE: They try to
kill you with fees,

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:23.610
taxes, regulations, hoops to
jump through, inspections.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:28.648
They go 10 times overboard
than any other business.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:31.718
I wish for them to do
the same regulation

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.119
to an alcohol company.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.325
So why operate a legal
business if you're not

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.895
even making money out of that?

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.363
GEORGE: For the love of it.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.899
Why do artists like to paint?

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.433
Or why does a
singer like to sing?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.036
I roll with the punches now
and just hanging in there

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:53.106
so that big business
doesn't just take

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.208
all the original people out.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.210
You know, you don't
feel comfortable with even

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.611
being in the same room.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:03.716
Why do you think there's
so much fear and mistrust?

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:06.920
GEORGE: It's kind of
ingrained in our culture.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.421
You can't really trust people.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.690
And that just comes
with money and greed.

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:15.028
And when people are
greedy, bad things happen.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.896
Do you carry a gun?

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:18.264
GEORGE: I have guns.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.033
Robberies happen left and right.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.435
In a situation if
you get robbed,

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.838
you really have no
choice but to use it.

